# Project Rules for wheelSpin

## Git workflow
- Do NOT run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or any other git write operations.
- It is fine to run read-only git commands (e.g. `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`) to inspect state.
- After making code changes, verify locally (e.g. `npm run build`, `npm run lint`) and let the user
  know the changes are ready. The user will review, stage, commit, and push themselves.

## Status tracking
- Keep `docs/status.md` up to date after meaningful chunks of work: check off completed items,
  add new items as they're discovered, and log notable decisions in the "Notes / Decisions Log"
  section with a date.
- See `docs/project-plan.md` for the original requirements/plan.
